Sam (CSM): Post-onboard check-in for Northwind. Mobile SDK rolled to beta and they saw a spike of 429s right after a feature flag flip. They're nervous since renewal is in two weeks.

Nina (Support Eng): Any logs or UA? 429 right after flag flips usually means many clients calling init/token fetch at once.

Sam (CSM): Customer log: `2026-03-21T08:12:01Z WARN preflight deny tenant=northwind count=138 window=1s` followed by many client-side `init()` failures.

Hao (DevEx): Sounds like ephemeral token fanout from mobile clients reconnecting. Quick ask: are they using background refresh on app resume?

Sam (CSM): Yes — they enabled aggressive session refresh on resume.

Eli (Solutions Eng): Mitigations: a) reduce client refresh frequency, b) share token across app instances when possible, c) add randomized jitter on resume (200ms-2s). Also implement exponential backoff for 429s.

Nina (Support Eng): Quick retry snippet we suggested:
```js
let tries=0;
function initSafe(){
  tries++;
  sdk.init().catch(e=>{
    if(e.status===429 && tries<6){
      setTimeout(initSafe, Math.min(2000, 100*Math.pow(2,tries)) + Math.random()*300);
    }
  });
}
initSafe();
```

Sam (CSM): Customer asked if we can temporarily raise tenant preflight quota while they roll fixes.

Eli (Solutions Eng): We can do a short bump 4x for 6 hours. Ops needs CR. I'll coordinate monitoring.

ops-bot: CR-8001 opened for tenant northwind: preflight quota bump 4x, window 10:00-16:00 UTC. Notifying #eng-oncall.

Hao (DevEx): I'll add a note to onboarding docs: "Avoid aggressive token refresh on app resume; prefer lazy refresh with jitter and reuse tokens across sessions."

Sam (CSM): I'll communicate plan to customer, emphasize app change is primary fix and quota bump is temporary. Will update here after validation so we can close CR-8001.
